							4 Nov. 1988.

Hi,

	This is the read me file for the document diskette.

	Contained on this diskette are the complete files for the TeX
source. All TeX files used are called *.tex. All Modified C source code
is called *.?t. I say modified because the is a bug (YES!!) in my TeX
verbatim listing macro, and if a line has a TAB as the first character,
it is thrown away. Hence, all lines that start with a TAB have got a space
inserted at the front of the line.

	A more serious reason that these *.?t files can't be used with the
compiler is that there have been carriage returns inserted at the 80th column
to stop overfull hbox errors with the \obeylines verbatim listings. So if
you want files for compiling, see the other diskette.

	To typeset the thesis, type at the operating system prompt:

			tex thesis

and this will do all the work and include all the files. To print
out the typeset version, see your system administrator, as this varies widly
from system to system.

	Thanks. And good luck with printing!

Scott MacGibbon.

P.S. This is the very latest version. Hence it includes A.2.6 net_type.h in
the correct spot, not as an after-thought as in the original.

P.P.S. Some implementations have different names for fonts. If the ones in
theader.tex are not right for your system, (and TeX will tell you very swiftly
if they are not) change them for the right ones. The usual problem is with
am* fonts instead of cm* fonts.

